"== Dark Ornamental #01 =="
$r = (RUN 'SHOW_IT {"subject": "Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: A towering Gothic cathedral structure built vertically from pointed arches, narrow columns and black tracery, tapering naturally as it descends. Monumental, Gothic, sacred. In the right panel it is on a man, full spine from upper back toward lower back. Create exceptional contemporary Dark Ornamental tattoo artwork designed specifically around human anatomy. DARK ORNAMENTAL = THE BODY DECORATED WITH DARK STRUCTURE. The ornament itself may be the entire subject. Draw from: Gothic architecture Cathedral tracery Pointed arches Wrought iron Dark jewelry Filigree Lace Thorns Blades Spikes Chains Botanical structures Sacred geometry Historical ornament Medieval engraving Woodcut textures Negative space Heavy blackwork Architectural repetition Do not automatically include: Skulls Faces Animals Demons Flowers Eyes Literal Gothic objects They may appear when conceptually appropriate, but Dark Ornamental does not require a conventional central subject. Avoid making 100 versions of the same symmetrical sternum tattoo. Vary: Scale Density Line weight Black coverage Symmetry Asymmetry Historical influence Body location Movement Negative space Gender presentation Composition Some pieces should be extremely fine. Some should be brutally heavy. Some should resemble jewelry. Some should resemble architecture. Some should resemble armor. Some should resemble ancient engraving. Some should feel contemporary and almost futuristic. Some should cover enormous portions of the body. DESIGN FROM THE BODY OUTWARD. Do not design a flat ornament and then find somewhere to put it. The shoulder should influence the design. The chest should influence the design. The sternum should influence the design. The spine should influence the design. The hips should influence the design. The joints should influence the design. The musculature should influence the design. For every design create: LEFT CARD: The complete tattoo artwork isolated on clean bright white. RIGHT CARD: The exact same artwork professionally tattooed on the specified real human body. Do not redesign between cards. Use realistic adult men and women with varied bodies and skin tones. Show enough of the persons body to understand why the placement works. The tattoo must appear genuinely integrated into skin. The human should look aspirational and contemporary. THE BODY IS NOT THE BACKGROUND. THE BODY IS THE ARCHITECTURE. DARK ORNAMENTAL = THE BODY DECORATED WITH DARK STRUCTURE. The tattoo in both panels is identical.", "raw": true, "aspect": "3:2"}' | Out-String)
$u = [regex]::Match($r, "https://auras\.guide/image/img_[a-z0-9]+").Value; if ($u) { "  look at it: " + $u } else { "  FAILED: " + $r.Substring(0,[Math]::Min(300,$r.Length)) }
"== Biomechanical #01 =="
$r = (RUN 'SHOW_IT {"subject": "Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: The shoulder appears partially opened to reveal an intricate titanium ball-and-socket joint surrounded by cables, pistons and layered mechanical structures. Powerful, mechanical, convincing. In the right panel it is on a man, shoulder and upper arm. Create extraordinary contemporary Biomechanical tattoo artwork. CORE PRINCIPLE: THE HUMAN BODY IS THE FOUNDATION. THE MACHINE IS THE IMAGINATION. Biomechanical is not a collection of gears. Biomechanical asks: WHAT ELSE COULD THIS BODY BE MADE OF. Explore: Mechanical anatomy Artificial bones Synthetic muscles Cybernetic joints Advanced machinery Bio-organic structures Alien anatomy Chrome Titanium Ceramic Carbon structures Translucent materials Iridescent surfaces Cables Tendons Hydraulics Artificial vertebrae Mechanical ribs Synthetic organs Energy systems Living machinery Impossible evolution Approximately 65 to 70 percent of body presentations should feature men. Approximately 30 to 35 percent should feature women. Use varied adult ages, body types and skin tones. Do not make female Biomechanical synonymous with delicate. Women can carry enormous, aggressive, strange and sophisticated biomechanical work. VARY BODY PLACEMENT AGGRESSIVELY. Use: Shoulders Upper arms Forearms Hands Chest Full torso Ribs Back Spine Shoulder blades Neck Hips Thighs Knees Calves Ankles Full legs Avoid endless sleeves. Avoid endless ripped-skin windows. Avoid endless gears. Avoid generic robot imagery. Avoid making every machine grey. Avoid simply drawing a robot on someones body. THE BODY ITSELF SHOULD APPEAR TRANSFORMED. Some pieces should look: Industrial Sleek Alien Organic Brutal Beautiful Luxurious Futuristic Predatory Minimal Massive Colorful Dark Elegant Terrifying Use torn-skin illusion only when it improves the concept. Other designs should transition seamlessly between human and machine. Some should appear beneath skin. Some should replace anatomy. Some should grow from anatomy. Some should behave like an exoskeleton. Some should look like an entirely new biological system. Some should make the viewer unsure whether the structure is mechanical or alive. The tattoo in both panels is identical.", "raw": true, "aspect": "3:2"}' | Out-String)
